Monday Update
* Trade Alert: Buy DKNG calls, AAL puts*&nbsp;Stocks rip higher as Treasury=
 market simmers downStocks are rising today as government bond yields fall =
and President Joe Biden's $1.9 trillion stimulus program passes through the=
 House of Representatives.The Dow Jones Industrial Average rose 2.2%, the S=
&amp;P 500 was higher by 2.4% and the Nasdaq Composite up by 2.6%. Energy, =
materials and utilities were among the biggest gainers, with all sectors in=
 the green after midday on Monday.The COVID-19 relief package, which now mo=
ves onto the Senate, includes means-tested payments of up to $1,400, boosts=
 unemployment payments and offers additional support for food stamps. The s=
timulus, which may lose a built-in $15 minimum wage proposal during the Sen=
ate approval process, has the potential to boost inflation, which drove the=
 sharp rally in government bond yields in recent weeks.The U.S. 10-year yie=
ld fell by 1.8 basis points to 1.44% intraday after touching a high of 1.61=
% last week. This momentum in yields triggered valuation concerns, especial=
ly in relation to technology shares, which have been market leaders during =
the COVID-19 pandemic environment. The Nasdaq jumped the most since early F=
ebruary on Monday.The Institute for Supply Management's U.S. manufacturing =
index rose to 60.8 in February from 58.7 in January. There were gains in th=
e measure for new orders, production, employment and prices. Readings above=
 50 mark expansion.In company news, Johnson &amp; Johnson (JNJ) rose by 1.2=
% as the drugmaker commenced the rollout of its one-dose coronavirus vaccin=
e, the third to be approved for emergency use in the U.S., to distribution =
centers and pharmacies across the country.NRG Energy (NRG) on Monday mainta=
ined its fiscal 2021 expectations of between $2.4 billion and $2.6 billion =
in adjusted earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortization, w=
ith investors sidestepping the decline in sales and earnings in the full-ye=
ar 2020. The shares surged by 16% intraday, the most on S&amp;P 500.&nbsp;O=
n the Dow, the top performer was Boeing (BA), with shares up by 5.9%. Morga=
n Stanley (MS) adjusted the price target on the stock to $250 to $230 while=
 maintaining the overweight ratingPortfolio: Our Cigna March 210 calls were=
 sold last week a 51.3% overall gain. We sold the first half of our ORCL ca=
lls Friday morning for a 27% gain and the rest at +3% on stop. WW and SBUX =
call orders did not fill Friday. ... We have two new ideas for you. One is =
puts on an airline; go lighter on this than usual as it is more speculative=
 than our typical offering.*CURRENT RECOMMENDATIONSOracle Corp. (ORCL) Marc=
h $60 calls-- Symbol: ORCL210319C00060000-- Bought at $5.15 on Feb. 22-- So=
ld half today at $6.55 fora 27.4% gain!-- Now trading at $5.90-- Second hal=
f sold Friday at $5.30 on stop for a gain of 3%.-- This trade is complete.*=
NEW RECOMMENDATIONSDraftKings Inc. (DKNG) March $65 calls-- Symbol: DKNG210=
319C00065000-- Order: Buy at $4.40 lmt day only-- If filled, set up to sell=
 half at $5.75 lmt gtc and half at $7.70 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at $=
3.10 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only&nbsp;*American Airlines Group (AAL)=
 March $23 puts-- Symbol: AAL210319P00023000-- Order: Buy at $2.40 lmt day =
only-- If filled, set up to sell half at $3.15 lmt gtc and half at $4.10 lm=
t gtc-- If filled, set stop at $1.70 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*Tha=
nks for reading,Jon D. MarkmanAll recommendations are for monthly options e=
xpiring on the third Friday of the specified month unless otherwise noted. =
